# Caddyfile.collapsed — Front_Proxy for the two-container-test-harness collapsed topology.
#
# Property 4, single-container parity (Req 4.2 / PARITY-COLLAPSE-29). The collapsed run is the
# same image, the same service definition, and the same volumes as the split run — it is an
# env-and-config overlay run.mjs applies on top of the reused `auth-surface` service, NOT a third
# topology. "No source change, no rebuild" is therefore a property of compose.harness.yml (one
# ${HARNESS_IMAGE} reference, one reused service) rather than an assertion about this file. This
# file's only job is to route every request to that one container.
#
# One unconditional upstream, NO allowlist. There is nothing to partition: the collapsed
# configuration runs a single container with startup tasks on and the full-access credential
# (run.mjs's env overlay), so every path resolves to it.
#
# It still sets X-Harness-Upstream, so the collapsed run reports attribution in the SAME shape as
# the split run — the parity checks read one header on both topologies rather than a header on one
# and its absence on the other.
#
# Like Caddyfile.split, the proxy performs NO credential validation of any kind — no bearer check,
# no cookie exemption, no crypto at the edge (NG6). It stands in for the Load_Balancer only and does
# not emulate the Auth_Gate.

{
	admin off
	auto_https off
}

:80 {
	# JSON access log to stdout, matching Caddyfile.split's shape so both topologies emit the same
	# access-log records for the runner to read.
	log {
		output stdout
		format json
	}

	# The collapsed upstream is the reused `auth-surface` service (compose.harness.yml's
	# proxy-collapsed points here). Same upstream address/port shape as Caddyfile.split
	# (auth-surface:3080). No `route`, no matcher, no allowlist — one unconditional handler for
	# every path.
	#
	# X-Harness-Upstream is set in the same block that picks the upstream, so the header and the
	# routing decision are one directive pair and cannot disagree. `header` replaces rather than
	# appends, so the value is the proxy's regardless of what the upstream emitted.
	handle /__harness/health {
		# Harness liveness probe for the proxy itself. Not part of the routed traffic; matches
		# Caddyfile.split's responder.
		respond "OK" 200
	}

	handle {
		header X-Harness-Upstream "auth-surface"
		reverse_proxy auth-surface:3080
	}
}
